    "vernacular": "Equatorial island nation (21 km2, no rivers; roofs double as rain catchment). Low one- and two-storey buildings of rendered concrete block painted white, cream or pastel, under corrugated or sheet-metal roofs (often red, green or grey), set on a narrow coastal belt of coconut palms and open white-coral sand; the interior is a limestone-pinnacle plateau of former phosphate mining. Public buildings are plain modern concrete boxes with flag poles; the tallest building on the island is a modest hotel block.",
