    "ornament": "Very little applied ornament: painted block walls, louvred and open-air shuttered windows for ventilation, deep eaves and verandas, flag poles. Traditional Nauruan crafts use coconut-fibre and geometric patterns but do not feature on buildings. Rusted Japanese WWII guns and concrete bunkers are the island's heritage markers.",
